    "summary": "Cloth, woman&#039;s wrapper, a single broad width, hand-woven from imported machine cotton with a pattern of coloured stripes against a purple background. The weft is of purple thread. Three quarters of the width of the cloth has warp stripes of  black, blue, green, yellow, and beige cotton. The remaining quarter of the cloth has no warp pattern, but instead a weft pattern extending only across a quarter of the width, using discontinuous lines of supplementary weft in three groups of three in lines of green, yellow, blue, black and white thread. Fringes have been left at both warp ends, and these have been twisted to form tassels.",
